,title,link,text,language,family
0,Aikanã language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aikanã_language,"Aikanã is an endangered language isolate spoken by about 200 Aikanã people in Rondônia, Brazil. It is morphologically complex and has SOV word order.",Aikanã,Language isolate
1,Aikanã | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/tba/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..GWc9RW9LS9R21M99Ld8C1bCMskTX9FsvC9I57E_5KJI,"Aikanã is an endangered indigenous language of Brazil. It is an isolate that is not known to be related to any other language. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people.",Aikanã,Language isolate
2,Indigenous languages in Brazil and the Corona epidemic. | Lingoblog,https://www.lingoblog.dk/en/indigenous-languages-​​in-brazil-and-the-corona-epidemic/,"Of the approximately 400 Aikanã, there are about 250 who speak the Aikanã language (an isolate also known as Massaka or Huari).The music of the purikɨi is also very special, because the sound represents words: songs and parts of the origin stories. You have to take that very literally.",Aikanã,Language isolate
3,Aikanã | Catalog,https://langsci-press.org/catalog/view/167/978/846-1,"The story of Fox is a myth told by different peoples of the southwestern Ama-zon, including the Aikanã. The Aikanã people speak an isolate language, which, with about 225 speakers out of an ethnic group of around 560, is to be con-sidered seriously endangered.",Aikanã,Language isolate
4,Aikanã language of Language Topics | Question AI,https://www.questionai.com/knowledge/kGmz3NrSIW-aikan-language,"Aikanã Tubarão, Huari Native to Brazil Region Rondônia Native speakers 150 (2012)e25 Language family Language isolate Dialects Masaká Language codes ISO 639-3 tba Glottolog aika1237 This article contains IPA phonetic symbols.",Aikanã,Language isolate
5,"Aikana Language and the Aikanã Indian Tribe (Tubarão, Masaka...)",https://www.native-languages.org/aikana.htm,"Language: Aikana is a language of South America, spoken by 100 people in Brazil. Some linguists believe it may be related to the Arawakan language family. Aikana is a morphologically complex tone language with many suffixes and primarily SOV word order.",Aikanã,Language isolate
6,Splitter AI — Isolate instruments from a song,https://vocalremover.org/splitter-ai,"AI-Powered Music Separator. This app allows to separate music into an individual streams such as vocal, bass, percussion, and lets you rebalance their individual volumes. This is the simplest way to get multitracks from any song.",Aikanã,Language isolate
7,definitely endangered language isolate spoken by about 200 Aikanã...,https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3409307,Language. Label. Description. Also known as. default for all languages. No label defined. – tba. English. Aikanã.0 references. linguistic typology. language isolate.,Aikanã,Language isolate
8,OLAC resources in and about the Aikanã language,http://olac.ldc.upenn.edu/language/tba,"Use faceted search to explore resources for Aikanã language. Primary texts. [Aikana field notes: Data book 1]. Carlson, Harvey (researcher); Espirito Santo, Luis (consultant); Sousa, Manoel Viera de (consultant); Viera de Sousa, Pedro (consultant); Viera de Sousa, Getulio (consultant).",Aikanã,Language isolate
9,I recognize you and I feel jealous.,https://naclo.org/resources/problems/2026/N2026-M.pdf,Aikanã is a language isolate spoken by around 150 people in western Brazil. Below are some sentences in Aikanã and their English translations.,Aikanã,Language isolate
